{"entryId":"1759","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1759:1","sourceSha256":"b496dadb5c1cd6645fd18dcd5ed6a696a733a82533315da82ed405628c338bbc","englishSha256":"ea4cc92c4b0618848be35ada9e40d967e58b7ced9f12a39b260bf78b8e56f82d","citations":[{"id":"1759:1:citation-01","he":[52,76],"en":[95,142],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_27b.6.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 27b:6:1","assessment":"The Mishnah says “on that day.” Rashi identifies the day as the appointment of Elazar ben Azaryah, and Berakhot independently connects the Eduyot session and the day formula.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 27b:6:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_27b.6.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Berakhot 28a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_28a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1759:1:citation-02","he":[94,227],"en":[263,312],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.14"},"reference":"Sotah 27b:14","assessment":"The same Mishnah names the speaker simply Rabbi Yehoshua. He addresses Rabban Yochanan ben Zakkai rhetorically and calls Akiva his student in one paragraph and Yehoshua ben Hyrcanus the student of his student in another. The respect motive and implied attendance are the compilation’s explanation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 27b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 27b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 27b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1759:1:citation-03","he":[229,283],"en":[447,495],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_27b.14.3"},"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 27b:14:3","assessment":"The checked Mishnah 5:5 and keyed Rashi on 27b support the Akiva student statement. The opening-chapter label is loose and is preserved.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 27b:14:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_27b.14.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"1759:1:citation-04","he":[342,397],"en":[497,558],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.5"},"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:5","assessment":"The received narrator’s argument turns on distinguishable name forms. The Mishnah supports the second form. The conjectural kinship and exclusion remain editorial arguments.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3],"holds":[{"raw":"אולי הוא אחיו הקטן של ר' אליעזר","reason":"The relationship remains the compilation’s conjecture.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"raw":"ואז היה ר\"א בלוד","reason":"The sourced general Lod association does not date his presence to the specific day.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 32b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_32b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"מפני כבודו אף שהיה ג\"כ תלמיד תלמידו","reason":"The motive and precise chain are Heilprin’s explanation of changed terminology.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sotah 27b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 27b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 27b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"כי בנו של ר\"א נקרא ר' הורקנוס","reason":"The comparative reference to Eliezer’s son lacks a precise cited witness here.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The named speaker in the Mishnah is Rabbi Yehoshua. The presence in Lod that day, motive of respect, and possible kinship remain the compiler’s claims.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Sotah 5:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Sotah_5.5"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 27b:6:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_27b.6.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Berakhot 28a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_28a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 32b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_32b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 27b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 27b:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sotah 27b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sotah_27b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Sotah 27b:14:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Sotah_27b.14.3"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
